{"name":"Thousand Sons Blue","hex":"#02d8e9","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"thousand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO, ICAO, ITU & IMO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for  thousand."]},{"part":"Numeral","definitions":["A numerical value equal to 1,000; ten times a hundred (1 E+3 exactly—in scientific E notation)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thousand"},{"term":"sons","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of son"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sons"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Warhammer 40,000","blocks":[{"text":"Warhammer 40,000, is a British miniature wargame produced by Games Workshop. It is the most popular miniature wargame in the world, and is particularly popular in the United Kingdom. The first edition of the rulebook was published in September 1987; the eleventh and current edition was released in June 2026."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Keno_mini_wargame.jpg/330px-Keno_mini_wargame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warhammer_40%2C000","wikidata":"Q209026"},{"title":"Son","blocks":[{"text":"A son is a male offspring; a boy or a man in relation to his parents. The female counterpart is a daughter. From a biological perspective, a son constitutes a first degree relative."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Son","wikidata":"Q177232"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Keno_mini_wargame.jpg/500px-Keno_mini_wargame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Keno_mini_wargame.jpg/500px-Keno_mini_wargame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKeno_mini_wargame.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg/500px-Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg/1280px-Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg/500px-Operation_Sci-Fi_Con_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOperation